# Proteus — Cursor / AI coding conventions

You are working in **Proteus**, a lightweight Kube-native backup & disaster-recovery system written in Rust.

## Architecture

- Cargo workspace under `crates/` + install under `deploy/`:
  - `proteus-core` — CAS engine
  - `proteus-crd` — CRD types (`kube-derive`)
  - `proteus-api` — Axum API + embedded UI assets
  - `proteus-controller` — Kubernetes operator
  - `proteus-ui` — Dioxus WASM control plane
  - `deploy/` — Dockerfile + Kustomize
- Target: Kubernetes **1.26+** (single cluster for MVP), Rust edition **2021**, async-first with **Tokio**.
- MVP: embedded UI, PVC-centric backups, single cluster; install via image and/or Kustomize.
- **100% Rust** including UI (Dioxus WASM). No Node/React/Vite application code.

## Craft (Clean Code + SOLID / Fowler / GoF) — non-negotiable

SOLID and Clean Code are review/merge criteria, not optional style.

- **S** Single Responsibility — one reason to change per type/module; no god files.
- **O** Open/Closed — extend via traits/new types; avoid editing cores for every variant.
- **L** Liskov — trait impls honor the contract; no surprise weaker invariants.
- **I** Interface Segregation — narrow traits; no fat interfaces callers half-use.
- **D** Dependency Inversion — depend on abstractions; wire concretes at the edge.
- Express intent in **names and structure**, not comments.
- Comments only for non-obvious **why** (trade-offs, invariants, external constraints).
- Do **not** add `///` on every item. No `#![deny(missing_docs)]`.
- Prefer small modules and clear types. Apply GoF patterns only when they remove real duplication or branching pain.
- Boy Scout rule on every touch.

## Error handling

- Libs: `thiserror`. Binary edge: `anyhow` OK.
- Never `unwrap` / `expect` / `panic!` in production paths.

## Async

- Tokio for I/O. Do not block the runtime.

## Kubernetes / CRDs

- Group `proteus.io`, version `v1alpha1`. Kinds: Repository, Backup, Restore.
- Reconcile idempotently; typed status updates.

## Style

- `cargo fmt` + `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --exclude proteus-ui -- -D warnings` before merge.
- Prefer composable modules over god files.
